  "worked_solution": "We can estimate the required value by substituting $x=16$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =27-0.5x \\\\  & =27-0.5(16) \\\\  & =27-8 \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=16,$ we have $y≈19.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=16$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
